{"id":"2a15e4e82341ff69","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-interpretation.md","title":"Interpretation","display":"df-interpretation — Interpretation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-interpretation","aliases":["93-df-interpretation"],"display":"df-interpretation — Interpretation","depends_on":["[[93-df-formula]]","[[93-df-logic]]","[[93-df-substitution]]","[[93-df-similarity-type]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-interpretation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-interpretation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-interpretation — Interpretation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c2ca1af9af149e69\" href=\"?note=c2ca1af9af149e69\" title=\"93-df-formula\">93-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8e602c19b2984096\" href=\"?note=8e602c19b2984096\" title=\"93-df-substitution\">93-df-substitution</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1\">\\(\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1\\)</span> are logic-pair candidates on a shared propositional formula algebra.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}\">\\(\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}\\)</span> have their sourced meanings; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\widehat I^{\\tau}\">\\(\\widehat I^{\\tau}\\)</span> is the type-indexed extension of the variable substitution <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}\\)</span> is the consequence interpretation predicate defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}interpretation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}(I,\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_0\\;\\exists\\vdash_1\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land F=T_{\\tau}(\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathcal L_0=\\langle F,\\vdash_0\\rangle\n\\land\\mathcal L_1=\\langle F,\\vdash_1\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_0)\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}(I;\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash_0\\varphi\\leftrightarrow\n\\widehat I^{\\tau}[\\Gamma]\\vdash_1\\widehat I^{\\tau}(\\varphi))\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}interpretation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}(I,\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_0\\;\\exists\\vdash_1\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land F=T_{\\tau}(\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathcal L_0=\\langle F,\\vdash_0\\rangle\n\\land\\mathcal L_1=\\langle F,\\vdash_1\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_0)\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}(I;\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash_0\\varphi\\leftrightarrow\n\\widehat I^{\\tau}[\\Gamma]\\vdash_1\\widehat I^{\\tau}(\\varphi))\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This book-local notion is a compositional interpretation between consequence relations on one propositionally generated formula algebra. The shared signature and both consequence relations are bound internally, so the three-place predicate has no ambient structural parameters.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"c2ca1af9af149e69","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-logic]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-substitution","status":"resolved","id":"8e602c19b2984096","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-substitution]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-similarity-type","status":"resolved","id":"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-similarity-type]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\widehat I^{\\tau}","display":false},{"tex":"I","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}interpretation}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Interp}_{93}(I,\\mathcal L_0,\\mathcal L_1)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_0\\;\\exists\\vdash_1\\;\\Bigl[{}&\n\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land F=T_{\\tau}(\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&\\land\\mathcal L_0=\\langle F,\\vdash_0\\rangle\n\\land\\mathcal L_1=\\langle F,\\vdash_1\\rangle\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_0)\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{Sub}_{93}(I;\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash_0\\varphi\\leftrightarrow\n\\widehat I^{\\tau}[\\Gamma]\\vdash_1\\widehat I^{\\tau}(\\varphi))\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1758,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["c2ca1af9af149e69","bd7e4207897c8db3","8e602c19b2984096","ee84ed8b0fae5bc3"]}